# Shepherd

`restore-fedora/.local/bin/shepherd` is the theme menu. Stow links it to `~/.local/bin/shepherd`. Packs live in `extra/themes/<name>/` and are not stowed. The script resolves its symlink back to the repo.

```
extra/themes/<name>/
  theme.conf     # only the fields the user picked
  vicinae/       # theme file and its icon, when picked
  <name>.colors  # KDE scheme, when picked; accent comes from its selection color
  gtk/           # GTK theme directory, when picked
  vscode/        # one .vsix, installed into both VS Code and Cursor
  firefox/       # Firefox addon, when picked
  helium/        # Helium addon, when picked
  wallpapers/    # images, when picked; apply uses the first file
```

The menu is `1` apply theme and `2` create theme.

Apply writes the pack into the live configs:

- Install the `.colors` file and apply it by its file name. Plasma matches that name, not the Name field inside the file. Set the wallpaper to the first image. Leave the look-and-feel and the Kaze-dark icon theme alone, on KDE and on Vicinae.
- Set `gtk-theme-name` in GTK 2, 3, and 4. Install `gtk/` into `~/.themes` when the pack has one. Do not change the icon theme.
- Set Ghostty only when a name was picked. Copy the Vicinae theme file into the Vicinae themes folder and select it. Install the `.vsix` into both editors and set the same color theme. Skip any piece the pack does not have.
- Read the Starship accent from the KDE scheme. Use the selection color when it contrasts with the window background; otherwise use the focus or link color that does. Skip Starship when no `.colors` file was picked.
- Recolor every Starship prompt color with the accent, including both glyphs and the directory path.
- Install the Firefox and Helium addons into the live profiles and select them. Firefox's profile comes from `profiles.ini`. Helium's profile is `~/.config/net.imput.helium/Default`. Both apply on the next launch of that browser. If Helium is open, do not write its preferences.

Do not invent addon files, color schemes, or wallpapers. Create only copies what the user points at.
